[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/comments/1086138204","html_url":"https://github.com/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/4058#issuecomment-1086138204","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/4058","id":1086138204,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAB-LNc5AvSdc","user":{"login":"miles-grant-ibigroup","id":86619099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NjE5MDk5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86619099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miles-grant-ibigroup","html_url":"https://github.com/miles-grant-ibigroup","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miles-grant-ibigroup/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miles-grant-ibigroup/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miles-grant-ibigroup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miles-grant-ibigroup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miles-grant-ibigroup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miles-grant-ibigroup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miles-grant-ibigroup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miles-grant-ibigroup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miles-grant-ibigroup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-04-01T16:59:21Z","updated_at":"2022-04-01T17:04:04Z","body":"The GTFS-RT spec marks `start_date` as conditionally required, which does not match OTP's claims. Removing the warning and replacing it like follows results in the bug being fixed.\r\n\r\n\r\n```java\r\nif (localDate.isEmpty()) {\r\n            localDate = Optional.of(new ServiceDate());\r\n        }\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever, I am weary of using this as a solution as there may be strange edge cases around midnight or an OTP server running in a different time zone than the feed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/comments/1086138204/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/comments/1086332804","html_url":"https://github.com/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/4058#issuecomment-1086332804","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/4058","id":1086332804,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAB-LNc5AwB-E","user":{"login":"barbeau","id":928045,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODA0NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/928045?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau","html_url":"https://github.com/barbeau","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-04-01T21:17:40Z","updated_at":"2022-04-01T21:17:40Z","body":">The GTFS-RT spec marks start_date as conditionally required\r\n\r\nThis is correct - [the spec](https://github.com/google/transit/blob/master/gtfs-realtime/spec/en/reference.md#message-tripdescriptor) says:\r\n\r\n>The initially scheduled start time of this trip instance. When the trip_id corresponds to a non-frequency-based trip, this field should either be omitted or be equal to the value in the GTFS feed. When the trip_id correponds to a frequency-based trip defined in GTFS frequencies.txt, start_time is required and must be specified for trip updates and vehicle positions. If the trip corresponds to exact_times=1 GTFS record, then start_time must be some multiple (including zero) of headway_secs later than frequencies.txt start_time for the corresponding time period. If the trip corresponds to exact_times=0, then its start_time may be arbitrary, and is initially expected to be the first departure of the trip. Once established, the start_time of this frequency-based exact_times=0 trip should be considered immutable, even if the first departure time changes -- that time change may instead be reflected in a StopTimeUpdate. If trip_id is omitted, start_time must be provided. Format and semantics of the field is same as that of GTFS/frequencies.txt/start_time, e.g., 11:15:35 or 25:15:35.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/comments/1086332804/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/comments/1086665703","html_url":"https://github.com/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/4058#issuecomment-1086665703","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/4058","id":1086665703,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAB-LNc5AxTPn","user":{"login":"hannesj","id":698100,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5ODEwMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/698100?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hannesj","html_url":"https://github.com/hannesj","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hannesj/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hannesj/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hannesj/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hannesj/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hannesj/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hannesj/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hannesj/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hannesj/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hannesj/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-04-02T15:47:11Z","updated_at":"2022-04-02T15:47:11Z","body":"On the actual field, `start_date`, it confusingly says, that it must be provided, but then states that it can be omitted:\r\n\r\n>The start date of this trip instance in YYYYMMDD format. For scheduled trips (trips not defined in GTFS frequencies.txt), this field must be provided to disambiguate trips that are so late as to collide with a scheduled trip on a next day. For example, for a train that departs 8:00 and 20:00 every day, and is 12 hours late, there would be two distinct trips on the same time. This field can be provided but is not mandatory for schedules in which such collisions are impossible - for example, a service running on hourly schedule where a vehicle that is one hour late is not considered to be related to schedule anymore. This field is required for frequency-based trips defined in GTFS frequencies.txt. If trip_id is omitted, start_date must be provided.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/comments/1086665703/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/comments/1086669607","html_url":"https://github.com/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/4058#issuecomment-1086669607","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/4058","id":1086669607,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAB-LNc5AxUMn","user":{"login":"barbeau","id":928045,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODA0NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/928045?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau","html_url":"https://github.com/barbeau","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barbeau/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-04-02T16:07:58Z","updated_at":"2022-04-02T16:07:58Z","body":"Ah, sorry, I see I copied the text for the wrong field start_time in my comment above.\r\n\r\nAgreed, that text could be clearer. It's trying to say that for schedule-based trips in the case where you could potentially have two TripUpdates for the same trip_id in service at the same time for service that overlaps more than one day, you must include start_date to disambiguate them. Otherwise for schedule-based trips it's optional (unless you omit trip_id).\r\n\r\nSo for schedule-based trips it's only required in a corner case.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/comments/1086669607/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/comments/1087198213","html_url":"https://github.com/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/4058#issuecomment-1087198213","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/4058","id":1087198213,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAB-LNc5AzVQF","user":{"login":"leonardehrenfried","id":151346,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTM0Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151346?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried","html_url":"https://github.com/leonardehrenfried","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-04-04T07:14:13Z","updated_at":"2022-04-04T07:14:13Z","body":"@hannesj An earlier version of the feature didn't need the start date since patterns can be looked up by id only. We added it because OTP adds internal copies of the pattern when there are realtime stop-time updates.\r\n\r\nWhat do you think about skipping the start date altogether, since it appears to be optional, and using the the `TripPattern`s id rather than the instance itself as the key [in the service](https://github.com/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/blob/cdb3e047a372c17414cf94ceab988340b6921eff/src/main/java/org/opentripplanner/routing/services/RealtimeVehiclePositionService.java#L12)?\r\n\r\nThis of course only works if the static and realtime pattern have the same id. Do they?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/comments/1087198213/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/comments/1088357382","html_url":"https://github.com/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/4058#issuecomment-1088357382","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/4058","id":1088357382,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAB-LNc5A3wQG","user":{"login":"leonardehrenfried","id":151346,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTM0Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151346?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried","html_url":"https://github.com/leonardehrenfried","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-04-05T07:28:17Z","updated_at":"2022-04-05T07:28:17Z","body":"I spoke to @hannesj yesterday and we agreed that I will implement a logic that tries to guess the correct service day from the available data.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/comments/1088357382/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/comments/1088359207","html_url":"https://github.com/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/4058#issuecomment-1088359207","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/4058","id":1088359207,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAB-LNc5A3wsn","user":{"login":"leonardehrenfried","id":151346,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTM0Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151346?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried","html_url":"https://github.com/leonardehrenfried","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-04-05T07:30:23Z","updated_at":"2022-04-05T07:30:23Z","body":"The reason that OTP needs the service day is that realtime stop time updates can internally create separate logical trips for each service day. We need to associate the vehicle position to the correct logic trip in order to return the correct data in the API.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/comments/1088359207/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/comments/1088721291","html_url":"https://github.com/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/4058#issuecomment-1088721291","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/issues/4058","id":1088721291,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAB-LNc5A5JGL","user":{"login":"leonardehrenfried","id":151346,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTM0Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151346?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried","html_url":"https://github.com/leonardehrenfried","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/leonardehrenfried/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-04-05T13:43:33Z","updated_at":"2022-04-05T13:43:33Z","body":"@miles-grant-ibigroup I've prepared a fix over at https://github.com/opentripplanner/OpenTripPlanner/pull/4066","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.